WEBVTT

00:05.714 --> 00:08.174
TOKYO REVENGERS

01:36.429 --> 01:42.435
The year's first meeting of all members
of the Tokyo Manji Gang will now begin!

01:42.519 --> 01:45.897
FIRST GENERATION TOKYO MANJI GANG

01:46.731 --> 01:50.568
Toman has been in conflict
with BLACK DRAGON a long time,

01:50.652 --> 01:53.113
but we had agreed to a truce.

01:53.947 --> 01:58.701
However, it was broken
due to strife between brothers,

01:59.244 --> 02:04.582
Second Division Vice-Captain Hakkai Shiba
and BLACK DRAGON leader Taiju Shiba.

02:05.375 --> 02:10.213
Then, due to independent action taken
by the two leaders of First Division,

02:10.797 --> 02:15.343
Second Division Captain Mitsuya,
and eventually, Mikey and I,

02:15.426 --> 02:20.181
fought and defeated Taiju Shiba
and all of BLACK DRAGON.

02:20.723 --> 02:24.811
Some members would like
to address everyone about this incident.

02:32.277 --> 02:34.779
First, Hakkai Shiba...

02:34.863 --> 02:35.822
Come forward!

02:46.541 --> 02:50.253
This all began... with my selfish lie.

02:51.963 --> 02:53.423
To maintain that lie,

02:54.215 --> 02:57.343
I dragged my family, Toman, into this.

02:58.595 --> 02:59.888
Things got out of hand

03:00.513 --> 03:03.183
and turned into war
between Toman and BLACK DRAGON.

03:04.517 --> 03:05.852
I'm to blame for it.

03:06.728 --> 03:07.562
Everyone...

03:08.229 --> 03:09.147
I apologize.

03:12.442 --> 03:13.651
Hakkai...

03:14.402 --> 03:15.528
What's this about?

03:15.612 --> 03:17.155
I don't really get it.

03:17.238 --> 03:18.531
What was the lie?

03:19.449 --> 03:21.492
Don't worry about it, Hakkai.

03:22.827 --> 03:24.495
Whatever sparks a conflict...

03:25.413 --> 03:27.957
It doesn't matter once it's all over.

03:28.041 --> 03:32.545
Besides, we defeated BLACK DRAGON.
Things turned out fine.

03:32.629 --> 03:34.172
Isn't that right, guys?

03:34.255 --> 03:35.423
That's right.

03:35.506 --> 03:37.133
Raise your head, Hakkai.

03:37.217 --> 03:40.929
I don't really get it,
but you've made a proper apology.

03:41.012 --> 03:42.472
You did good.

03:42.555 --> 03:43.848
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

03:45.558 --> 03:46.392
Guys...

03:48.019 --> 03:48.978
Hakkai.

03:49.062 --> 03:53.942
You will continue to be
vice-captain of Toman's Second Division.

03:54.525 --> 03:56.527
You're all cool with that, right?

03:56.611 --> 03:58.446
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

03:59.113 --> 04:00.949
-Hakkai!
-Hakkai!

04:01.032 --> 04:04.202
-Hakkai! Hakkai!
-Hakkai! Hakkai!

04:04.285 --> 04:05.870
-Hakkai!
-Hakkai!

04:05.954 --> 04:08.206
That fight with BLACK DRAGON was worth it

04:08.915 --> 04:12.752
just to save Hakkai,
wasn't it, Takemitchy?

04:13.294 --> 04:14.128
Yeah.

04:14.879 --> 04:19.759
Next, Seishu Inui
and Hajime Kokonoi, come forward.

04:28.851 --> 04:33.064
I am Seishu Inui
of the 11th generation BLACK DRAGON.

04:33.564 --> 04:36.025
And I'm Hajime Kokonoi of the same gang.

04:37.026 --> 04:38.236
BLACK DRAGON?

04:38.319 --> 04:40.029
I thought they were eliminated.

04:40.113 --> 04:43.324
The 10th generation BLACK DRAGON
lost to Toman.

04:44.033 --> 04:46.494
The leader, Taiju Shiba, retired.

04:47.120 --> 04:50.415
We've taken over
the 11th generation of BLACK DRAGON.

04:51.249 --> 04:53.584
And after negotiating with Mikey,

04:54.669 --> 04:56.921
we've decided to join under Toman.

04:57.005 --> 04:57.964
What?

04:58.047 --> 05:03.428
BLACK DRAGON will be assigned to
First Division, under Takemichi Hanagaki.

05:03.511 --> 05:05.388
-What?
-What?

05:05.471 --> 05:07.598
Got it, Takemitchy?

05:10.351 --> 05:13.730
BLACK DRAGON is going
to be under me? How come?

05:14.647 --> 05:16.566
Was that your decision, Mikey?

05:16.649 --> 05:19.319
I'm respecting their request.

05:20.069 --> 05:22.572
If they joined,
they wanted to be under you.

05:23.406 --> 05:25.408
They've definitely got an ulterior motive.

05:31.914 --> 05:33.916
Glad to be here, Captain.

05:35.126 --> 05:37.628
I won't ask you to trust us.

05:38.463 --> 05:40.423
But when you need help, let us know...

05:40.506 --> 05:41.799
and we'll help you.

05:47.180 --> 05:48.639
Silence!

05:50.183 --> 05:54.771
Lastly, I've got something to say
about the Christmas conflict.

05:55.355 --> 05:56.314
Mikey?

05:58.358 --> 05:59.776
Tetta Kisaki.

06:01.402 --> 06:02.236
Yes?

06:04.364 --> 06:05.823
I'm kicking you out.

06:06.991 --> 06:08.785
As of today, you're expelled.

06:12.163 --> 06:13.498
Kisaki's kicked out?

06:13.581 --> 06:14.707
No way.

06:15.833 --> 06:16.918
But how come?

06:21.756 --> 06:22.965
I told Mikey

06:23.049 --> 06:25.927
about how Kisaki betrayed us.

06:26.010 --> 06:26.886
You did?

06:26.969 --> 06:30.973
But I never thought Mikey would do this.

06:31.557 --> 06:35.520
He's risen to executive rank,
so I didn't think he'd get kicked out.

06:36.020 --> 06:40.108
That's insane, Mikey. You must be joking.

06:40.191 --> 06:42.652
You think I would joke here?

06:43.694 --> 06:44.821
You're out.

06:47.615 --> 06:50.243
Hey, hold on here, Mikey.

06:50.827 --> 06:54.163
If you kick Kisaki out,
then naturally, I'm leaving Toman too.

06:54.789 --> 06:55.832
In other words...

06:56.457 --> 07:00.378
Of the 450 members of Tokyo Manji Gang,

07:00.461 --> 07:02.422
the 50 former members of Moebius

07:02.964 --> 07:06.259
and all 300 former members
of Valhalla will drop out.

07:06.801 --> 07:10.430
That means Toman
will shrink to 100 members.

07:10.513 --> 07:12.223
Is that what you want?

07:12.306 --> 07:13.391
I don't care.

07:14.100 --> 07:16.436
Toman had gotten too big anyway.

07:16.519 --> 07:17.478
Huh?

07:18.771 --> 07:20.481
Gotten too big?

07:20.982 --> 07:25.486
That's insane, Mikey.
Isn't that Toman's objective?

07:25.570 --> 07:30.575
Then, was your objective in instigating
the Christmas conflict to grow Toman?

07:32.618 --> 07:34.328
Instigate the Christmas conflict?

07:34.412 --> 07:36.456
Was Kisaki also involved?

07:36.539 --> 07:38.624
Wasn't it just Division One and Two?

07:38.708 --> 07:44.338
You incited Takemitchy and them,
and gave Yuzuha a knife to kill Taiju.

07:44.881 --> 07:45.798
Isn't that right?

07:45.882 --> 07:48.176
Huh? What's this all about?

07:48.259 --> 07:50.678
Was Kisaki behind all of it?

07:50.761 --> 07:52.180
What? Damn scumbag!

07:53.139 --> 07:55.641
Did he think I wouldn't talk?

07:55.725 --> 07:59.479
I didn't think
Kisaki would get kicked out over this.

07:59.562 --> 08:01.606
There's no proof, after all.

08:01.689 --> 08:04.484
But I'd like to see
what excuses he comes up with.

08:05.693 --> 08:11.073
I've turned a blind eye to your
underhanded methods for growing Toman.

08:11.157 --> 08:12.909
But no longer.

08:16.329 --> 08:17.580
You've got it all wrong!

08:17.663 --> 08:19.332
You had grown weak.

08:19.874 --> 08:22.084
Taiju was a threat to Toman.

08:22.627 --> 08:24.587
I did that for your sake.

08:25.087 --> 08:25.922
Hey.

08:26.547 --> 08:28.925
Who said you could come forward?

08:32.011 --> 08:34.889
You listen to what Kisaki's got to say.

08:34.972 --> 08:36.182
You bastard.

08:40.561 --> 08:43.731
Don't listen to what
those losers say, Mikey.

08:44.398 --> 08:47.610
Aren't you going
to build an era for hoodlums?

08:47.693 --> 08:51.239
<i>Kisaki is actually panicking now.</i>

08:51.322 --> 08:56.285
Toman's going to grow huge.
We'll be a gang everyone bows to.

08:56.786 --> 08:59.330
When we get bigger,
it's sure to breed darkness.

08:59.413 --> 09:01.832
<i>Kisaki adored Mikey.</i>

09:01.916 --> 09:04.502
I'll take on all that darkness.

09:04.585 --> 09:09.674
<i>Kisaki's objective in that conflict
was to get Draken killed.</i>

09:09.757 --> 09:12.969
<i>Then he would take
the empty number-two spot.</i>

09:13.052 --> 09:14.512
You get it, right?

09:14.595 --> 09:18.558
<i>From the very start,
Kisaki joined Toman to get at Mikey.</i>

09:18.641 --> 09:20.434
I swear I'll be useful.

09:20.518 --> 09:22.353
<i>I know myself.</i>

09:22.436 --> 09:25.398
<i>The moon can't shine all by itself.</i>

09:25.481 --> 09:27.775
I'm here to make you shine.

09:30.611 --> 09:34.365
You need me, Mikey.

09:38.703 --> 09:41.205
I am the shadow that you cast.

09:42.623 --> 09:44.250
We need each other.

09:44.792 --> 09:46.877
Just reconsider, Mikey.

09:48.004 --> 09:50.965
You'll never achieve your dream
with high-minded babel.

09:58.681 --> 10:01.392
Hey, Takemitchy. He's lost it.

10:01.475 --> 10:03.728
<i>He's not talking sense.</i>

10:04.270 --> 10:07.648
<i>His feelings for Mikey are illogical.</i>

10:09.400 --> 10:11.027
We're through, Kisaki.

10:13.404 --> 10:15.698
Your rash assumptions
will screw up my dream.

10:16.574 --> 10:19.368
Mi... Mi...

10:22.538 --> 10:24.874
Mikey!

10:29.629 --> 10:30.880
<i>Kisaki...</i>

10:31.464 --> 10:33.299
<i>He's been expelled.</i>

10:36.218 --> 10:37.178
Lame.

10:37.845 --> 10:39.513
This meeting is over.

10:39.597 --> 10:40.556
Dismissed!

10:43.059 --> 10:44.143
<i>That was fast.</i>

10:44.685 --> 10:45.519
<i>Does this mean...</i>

10:46.228 --> 10:48.481
<i>Does this mean my mission was a success?</i>

10:58.991 --> 11:01.535
I'm beat. How's it look, Draken?

11:02.119 --> 11:03.412
Almost there.

11:04.955 --> 11:07.333
Mikey, try starting the engine.

11:17.343 --> 11:18.552
It started.

11:19.303 --> 11:20.846
All right, we're done.

11:27.603 --> 11:28.562
All right!

11:31.399 --> 11:33.693
I'm going to go get him.

11:33.776 --> 11:35.986
He's probably almost here.

11:36.612 --> 11:37.571
You just called.

11:37.655 --> 11:39.073
I can't wait.

11:40.074 --> 11:41.033
He's like a kid.

11:44.412 --> 11:46.789
Huh? What's this about?

11:46.872 --> 11:50.918
Just do it. Don't you let go yet, Chifuyu.

11:51.001 --> 11:52.044
You got it.

11:52.128 --> 11:53.754
This is really scary.

11:54.338 --> 11:55.673
Over here.

11:58.968 --> 12:00.052
Wow...

12:00.136 --> 12:02.680
Okay, open your eyes on zero.

12:03.597 --> 12:04.557
Five.

12:04.640 --> 12:05.474
Four.

12:05.558 --> 12:06.517
Three.

12:06.600 --> 12:07.435
Two.

12:07.518 --> 12:08.561
One.

12:08.644 --> 12:09.770
Zero.

12:09.854 --> 12:11.188
Ta-da!

12:13.566 --> 12:15.693
What? A bike?

12:15.776 --> 12:16.610
Yeah.

12:17.778 --> 12:21.115
It's a CB250T, also known as "Babu."

12:22.491 --> 12:24.034
It's the twin of mine.

12:24.535 --> 12:25.703
Twin...

12:26.537 --> 12:30.791
My brother found them
when he was traveling to buy parts.

12:31.792 --> 12:34.545
It was in some town in the Philippines.

12:36.130 --> 12:42.553
<i>He said he found the engine
for this one and for my own CB250T</i>

12:43.220 --> 12:44.388
<i>sad and alone in a junk heap.</i>

12:45.347 --> 12:46.557
Wow...

12:47.057 --> 12:51.937
He went around gathering parts
and revived mine.

12:52.563 --> 12:57.651
He didn't do anything with the other,
but Draken and I gathered parts.

12:58.319 --> 13:00.488
We finally just completed it.

13:00.571 --> 13:04.033
Really? That's so inspiring.

13:04.116 --> 13:05.201
It sure is.

13:06.452 --> 13:07.661
It's yours.

13:07.745 --> 13:08.579
Huh?

13:09.121 --> 13:14.043
It doesn't look good for the captain
of Division One not to have a bike.

13:14.126 --> 13:18.380
But this is such an important bike.
Why give it to me?

13:18.464 --> 13:20.633
It's a waste to just display it.

13:21.425 --> 13:25.554
Besides, we did ruin that thing
that was precious to you.

13:26.347 --> 13:27.181
That's right.

13:27.264 --> 13:29.809
But this is totally different than that.

13:32.019 --> 13:34.396
This is so awesome, Takemitchy!

13:35.189 --> 13:36.065
Yeah.

13:36.148 --> 13:37.691
Get on it.

13:37.775 --> 13:38.609
What?

13:43.864 --> 13:45.908
-Babu. Babu.
-Start it up.

13:45.991 --> 13:48.327
Huh? How do you do that?

13:48.410 --> 13:50.913
Here. I'll teach you.

13:53.666 --> 13:55.626
Drive around the block.

13:57.837 --> 14:01.757
No, Takemitchy.
That's wrong. You're still in first.

14:01.841 --> 14:02.800
Shift up!

14:03.634 --> 14:06.720
Release the accelerator
and squeeze the clutch!

14:06.804 --> 14:08.514
What? The clutch?

14:08.597 --> 14:10.140
I just showed you.

14:12.351 --> 14:14.144
That's the brake.

14:14.228 --> 14:15.813
Not that one. That one.

14:15.896 --> 14:19.859
I can't tell when you say "that one."
Tell me left or right.

14:19.942 --> 14:21.151
Why are you so mad?

14:21.235 --> 14:22.778
Oh, sorry.

14:22.862 --> 14:26.198
I told you, shift up with this foot.

14:26.282 --> 14:27.658
Like this?

14:27.741 --> 14:30.077
No! That's the brake.

14:30.160 --> 14:31.996
They're all brakes.

14:32.079 --> 14:33.289
What a thick skull.

14:38.210 --> 14:40.880
He sensed it was destiny.

14:41.380 --> 14:42.214
Huh?

14:42.965 --> 14:45.009
When he found the engines.

14:46.302 --> 14:49.054
<i>The sky was a suffocating gray.</i>

14:49.555 --> 14:53.517
<i>In an abandoned building
with a broken roof,</i>

14:54.935 --> 14:57.104
<i>he found these guys under the rubble.</i>

15:02.693 --> 15:05.821
He said they were calling to him.

15:06.530 --> 15:07.573
Really?

15:08.198 --> 15:10.242
I'd like to go there someday.

15:10.326 --> 15:11.577
Let's go there.

15:11.660 --> 15:15.122
Yeah. Okay, that's a promise, Takemitchy.

15:15.205 --> 15:16.123
Right.

15:24.006 --> 15:26.467
You're getting good, Takemitchy.

15:26.550 --> 15:29.470
Yeah. I think I got the hang of it.

15:44.318 --> 15:45.778
What you thinking about?

15:46.362 --> 15:47.196
Huh?

15:47.821 --> 15:50.282
Uh, well...

15:51.533 --> 15:53.243
I wonder what'll happen now.

15:54.161 --> 15:59.792
BLACK DRAGON is under us.
Kisaki and Hanma are out of Toman.

16:00.918 --> 16:04.463
Division One is the biggest in Toman now.

16:05.839 --> 16:08.759
Even if the ex-BLACK DRAGON guys
have an ulterior motive,

16:09.426 --> 16:12.930
Taiju didn't die
and Kisaki was kicked out of Toman.

16:14.056 --> 16:16.392
Your mission here is over.

16:18.018 --> 16:20.354
You're going back to the future, right?

16:22.106 --> 16:22.940
Yeah.

16:24.316 --> 16:25.275
Okay.

16:28.737 --> 16:29.738
This is goodbye.

16:31.240 --> 16:33.534
You belong 12 years in the future.

16:34.326 --> 16:35.160
Not here.

16:36.412 --> 16:40.457
Twelve years in the future,
where Hina and Akkun are still alive.

16:41.583 --> 16:43.961
I... I...

16:45.254 --> 16:46.463
Chifuyu!

16:47.047 --> 16:48.757
Thank you for everything!

16:49.341 --> 16:51.844
Without you,
I never would've made it this far!

16:52.428 --> 16:55.514
You're the best friend I've ever had!

17:03.439 --> 17:05.149
Let's meet again in 12 years.

17:06.567 --> 17:09.528
We'll be apart
just a short while until then.

17:19.663 --> 17:21.498
Sorry to make you come see me, Naoto.

17:22.207 --> 17:25.044
What's this important thing
you need to see me about?

17:26.045 --> 17:30.090
Naoto, I leave Hina in your hands.

17:34.762 --> 17:37.056
I know what I'm saying sounds strange.

17:37.806 --> 17:38.640
But...

17:39.641 --> 17:40.476
But?

17:43.353 --> 17:44.605
Take care of Hina.

17:49.943 --> 17:50.944
All right. I will.

17:52.112 --> 17:53.781
This is goodbye, Naoto.

18:00.162 --> 18:03.373
<i>I met with Mikey and them
one last time before that.</i>

18:06.543 --> 18:10.255
What's wrong, Takemitchy?
What'd you need to see us for?

18:10.756 --> 18:12.299
"Kisaki is the enemy."

18:13.550 --> 18:16.261
Those were Baji's final words to me.

18:18.555 --> 18:21.433
"The captain
of Division Three isn't Kisaki."

18:21.517 --> 18:22.726
"Only Pah is."

18:25.479 --> 18:26.313
"Pah-chin."

18:26.897 --> 18:28.065
"Mitsuya."

18:29.399 --> 18:30.234
"Draken."

18:30.859 --> 18:31.985
"Mikey."

18:33.320 --> 18:34.154
"Kazutora."

18:34.988 --> 18:36.198
"They're..."

18:37.324 --> 18:42.538
They're... my treasures.

18:45.999 --> 18:50.254
Please don't forget
what Baji was trying to achieve!

18:50.337 --> 18:52.381
Stay strong!

18:55.092 --> 18:58.470
Mikey, you can build
a new era on your own.

18:59.263 --> 19:00.681
Takemitchy...

19:10.274 --> 19:12.151
Quit making me cry, damn it.

19:14.486 --> 19:16.780
Can I ask for one more thing?

19:18.198 --> 19:19.825
How about a photo?

19:19.908 --> 19:20.909
Huh?

19:20.993 --> 19:22.077
What's the occasion?

19:23.996 --> 19:27.708
<i>I'll never see these guys
in the past again.</i>

19:28.584 --> 19:31.962
Come on. Why not? Gather in a group.

19:32.045 --> 19:33.338
How lame.

19:33.422 --> 19:34.506
You guys eaten?

19:34.965 --> 19:36.008
What a pain.

19:36.091 --> 19:37.092
Chifuyu!

19:39.428 --> 19:40.596
Here goes.

19:42.431 --> 19:45.976
Mikey! Everybody, look this way.

20:08.957 --> 20:12.252
<i>Where am I? A temple?</i>

20:14.671 --> 20:16.006
<i>I'm back.</i>

20:16.089 --> 20:17.049
JANUARY 10, 2018

20:17.132 --> 20:17.966
Oh.

20:19.176 --> 20:23.263
<i>In the previous timeline, I was in prison.</i>

20:23.347 --> 20:27.017
<i>Since I'm not incarcerated now,
things have changed.</i>

20:27.100 --> 20:29.645
<i>Then Hina's okay too.</i>

20:32.147 --> 20:33.273
Hanagaki.

20:33.357 --> 20:34.191
Huh?

20:34.816 --> 20:35.943
It's been a while.

20:36.693 --> 20:38.403
Oh, uh...

20:39.112 --> 20:40.030
<i>Who's she?</i>

20:41.448 --> 20:45.994
I know you're very busy,
but thank you for taking the time to come.

20:46.912 --> 20:48.038
Please, this way.

20:49.164 --> 20:50.123
<i>What's going on?</i>

20:54.753 --> 20:56.380
Please wait in this line.

20:57.047 --> 20:58.590
<i>A funeral?</i>

20:59.341 --> 21:01.301
<i>Well, I guess
I am wearing a mourning suit.</i>

21:02.552 --> 21:04.680
<i>But whose funeral is it?</i>

21:06.014 --> 21:10.644
<i>If that lady is at the reception table,
she must be a relative of the deceased.</i>

21:13.563 --> 21:14.481
Hanagaki.

21:16.650 --> 21:17.526
Huh?

21:17.609 --> 21:20.862
Thank you for coming to my brother's...

21:21.530 --> 21:22.364
<i>Brother?</i>

21:23.782 --> 21:26.994
<i>Wait a minute. I think I remember her.</i>

21:27.494 --> 21:28.954
Please, go inside.

21:29.037 --> 21:30.163
Okay.

21:33.083 --> 21:34.251
Pull yourself together, Mana.

21:34.960 --> 21:36.461
I'm sorry, Luna.

21:37.045 --> 21:38.964
<i>Mana? Luna?</i>

21:39.840 --> 21:40.674
<i>Brother...</i>

21:41.174 --> 21:42.009
Huh?

21:47.848 --> 21:48.807
<i>It can't be!</i>

21:59.401 --> 22:00.736
<i>No way...</i>

22:02.070 --> 22:03.071
